From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Nov 2026 07:50:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: leave the rotations the offline rotator does not
 take to the inline rotator

dpu_plane_rot_check() refuses every 90/270 plane the offline rotator
does not take (YUV, reflected) when the SoC has an offline rotator. That
was right while no such SoC had an SSPP inline rotator, but SM8250 has
both now: its VIG pipes rotate UBWC NV12 inline, which the offline
rotator does not take.

Where some SSPP has an inline rotator, return 0 for such a plane and
leave it to the normal path, which reserves a rotating pipe and checks
the format and the size. Packed RGB still goes to the offline rotator.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane_rot.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane_rot.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane_rot.c
index 03bcb91..08de53e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane_rot.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane_rot.c
@@ -204,6 +204,17 @@ static int dpu_plane_rot_check_geometry(struct drm_plane_state *new_plane_state,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool dpu_plane_rot_has_inline(const struct dpu_mdss_cfg *catalog)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < catalog->sspp_count; i++)
+		if (test_bit(DPU_SSPP_INLINE_ROTATION, &catalog->sspp[i].features))
+			return true;
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 int dpu_plane_rot_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
 			struct drm_plane_state *plane_state,
 			const struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state,
@@ -225,8 +236,14 @@ int dpu_plane_rot_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
 		return 0;
 	if (!crtc_state)
 		return 0;
+	/*
+	 * A rotation this rotator does not take (YUV, reflected) goes to an SSPP
+	 * inline rotator where there is one (SM8250: UBWC NV12), which the
+	 * normal path validates.
+	 */
 	if (!dpu_plane_rot_needed(dpu_kms, plane_state))
-		return (plane_state->rotation & (DRM_MODE_ROTATE_90 | DRM_MODE_ROTATE_270)) ? -EINVAL : 0;
+		return (plane_state->rotation & (DRM_MODE_ROTATE_90 | DRM_MODE_ROTATE_270)) &&
+		       !dpu_plane_rot_has_inline(catalog) ? -EINVAL : 0;
 
 	reqs.yuv = false;
 	reqs.scale = (plane_state->fb->height != drm_rect_width(&plane_state->dst)) ||
